git/      git 2.34 and libcurl3-gnutls, liberror-perl (Ubuntu jammy packages)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  git ................. GNU General Public License v2.0 (GPLv2), with some files
                        under LGPL v2.1+ (see git's COPYING and LGPL-2.1)
  libcurl3-gnutls ..... curl license (MIT/X derivative)
  liberror-perl ....... MIT-style (Error.pm, same terms as Perl: Artistic/GPL)

  WRITTEN OFFER OF SOURCE (GPLv2 section 3(b)):
  The git binaries in this pak are Ubuntu's unmodified builds of the source
  package `git` version <components.git> for Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy), extracted
  from the .deb with `dpkg -x`. The complete corresponding source code is
  published by Ubuntu at

      https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/git
      https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/jammy/+source/git/<version>

  and is obtainable on any Ubuntu 22.04 system with `apt-get source git`.
  In addition, for a period of three years from the date of each Build Pak
  release, anyone in possession of that release may obtain a copy of the
  complete corresponding source for git, libcurl3-gnutls and liberror-perl, on
  physical media for no more than the cost of shipping, by opening an issue at
  https://github.com/brianmiller/phvalheim-vibes-buildpak/issues with the pak
  version number. The GPLv2 text is at
  https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt and inside the Ubuntu
  source package (COPYING).

